  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Outside Golden Dawn Hall an old rank seven Gu Immortal dressed in a golden robe invites everyone to attack Hei tribe together, and other immortals recognize him as Gong Er. After a long silence with no Huang Jin response, Bai Zu tribe’s three Gu Immortals greet him and enter the hall, letting him save face.",
      "chapters": [
        1105
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_golden_dawn_hall",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "fac_bai_zu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is an old Gu Immortal dressed in a golden robe.",
      "chapters": [
        1105
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He presses Bai Zu tribe about entering Iron Eagle blessed land while ground resources are being fought over, and is surprised when they stay calm and wait.",
      "chapters": [
        1106
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blessed-land-watch",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "From Golden Dawn Hall he watches rainbow-colored fireworks of battle over the blessed land, records scenes with hidden Gu worms, grows impatient when no Hei tribe Gu Immortal appears, and orders Gong tribe immortals down to assist and preempt schemes while claiming Gong tribe leads the righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        1107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recording-and-descent",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "fac_gong_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He greets Heavenly Lord Bai Zu alone inside Iron Eagle blessed land. Though proud, he must be polite to a rank eight. He had wanted Golden Dawn Hall to snatch resources, but a warning from Prince Feng Xian stops him, and he leaves bitterly after failing to make other Huang Jin immortals treat him as righteous path leader.",
      "chapters": [
        1110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "bai-zu-humiliation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu",
        "char_prince_feng_xian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration recalls that Gong tribe suffered most at Iron Eagle blessed land and that Gong Er was punished when he returned to the tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "punished-after-iron-eagle",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
